# The runner's per-run state (verify/run.sh): local, and never part of the record.
.gate-state/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# A virtual environment, and what an install or a build makes, at a worktree's root: a parcel's own tools, never
# the record (P0.1's verifier, round 4, N5: the privacy gate read one, and failed on a third party's address; P0.2's
# verifier, round 1, G2: env/, build/ and .tox/ still did). Anchored at the root, all but *.egg-info/, which an
# install makes beside its package, wherever that is: so a directory of the other names below the root, a test's
# build/ under tests/ say, is still read, and still run.
/.venv/
/venv/
/env/
/build/
/dist/
/.tox/
*.egg-info/
